Case Study: End-to-End Flight Delay Data Engineering Pipeline

Business Problem

Airline operations generate millions of flight records every day from multiple systems in different formats such as CSV, JSON, and XML. These datasets contain valuable information about flight schedules, delays, cancellations, airports, and airlines.

However, the raw data has several challenges:

* Data arrives in multiple file formats.
* Data quality issues (null values, duplicates, inconsistent column names).
* Large volume (~25GB) makes manual processing inefficient.
* No centralized analytics layer for reporting.
* Difficult to track pipeline execution and data quality.

The organization needed a scalable, cloud-native data engineering solution to ingest, process, govern, and analyze flight delay data.

⸻

Objective

Build an end-to-end Medallion Architecture pipeline using Databricks that:

* Supports multi-format ingestion (CSV, JSON, XML)
* Handles incremental data loading
* Performs data cleansing and standardization
* Implements Delta Lake best practices
* Creates analytical Star Schema
* Provides monitoring dashboards
* Enables business reporting
